  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by virtue of the number of potential occupants and proposed use, would represent an over-intensification of the site which would be harmful to the amenities of the neighbouring properties and at odds with the established character of the surrounding locality. The proposal would have an unacceptable and undue impact on existing residential amenity in terms of noise and disturbance, over and above what would be expected for a single family dwelling. As such, the proposal would therefore be contrary to Policy EM8 of the Hillingdon Local Plan - Part 1: Strategic Policies (2012), Policies DMH 5 and DMHB 11 of the Hillingdon Local Plan: Part 2 - Development Management Policies (2020) and Policy D14 of the London Plan (2021).",
    "The proposed development, by virtue of its layout, internal design, number of potential occupants, and lack of adequate accessible private external amenity space, would present a living environment which would be neither comfortable or practical, nor fit for the intended purpose. Considered altogether, the proposed development would provide a sub-standard and unsatisfactory level of internal and external living accommodation for the future occupiers, contrary to Policy DMH 5 of the Hillingdon Local Plan: Part Two - Development Management Policies (2020) and Policies D3 and D6 of the London Plan (2021).",
    "In the absence of specific details and by virtue of its prominent, frontage siting and layout, which would be at odds with the prevailing form of development in the area, the proposal fails to effectively demonstrate that sufficient and suitable provision for well-designed storage refuse space and cycle space could be provided on-site, without causing harm to the visual character and appearance of the area.  As such, the proposal would be contrary to Policies DMH 5 and DMHB 11 of the Hillingdon Local Plan: Part Two - Development Management Policies (2020)."
  ],
